24: // === DSL attribute bindings (boundary-conditions wave) ===
25: //
26: // A kernel that declares `attr <domain> <type> <name>` fields opts those mesh
27: // attribute layers into the per-dab binding set. Codegen emits one
28: // BrushAttrManifestEntry per declared attr into BrushCommandDef::attrs; the
29: // executor resolves each to a live mesh layer (ensuring it exists) once per dab
30: // and exposes it through CommandCtxBase::boundAttr<T>().
31: 
32: // Which mesh element domain an attribute lives on (runtime mirror of the
33: // compiler-side sbrush::AttrDomain — kept separate so the runtime never depends
34: // on the DSL compiler headers).
35: enum class AttrElemDomain : int { Vertex, Face, Edge, Corner };
36: } // namespace sculptcore::brush
